    }
  },
  "icons": {
    "16": "icons/icon16.png",
    "48": "icons/icon48.png",
    "128": "icons/icon128.png"
  }
}
```

3. **Create the popup HTML** (`popup.html`): This is where users will interact with your extension.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <title>Save Page Content</title>
  <style>
    body { font-family: Arial, sans-serif; padding: 10px; }
    button { margin-top: 10px; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <h1>Save Current Page Content</h1>
  <button id="saveButton">Save</button>
  <script src="popup.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
```

4. **Create the popup JavaScript** (`popup.js`): This script handles the logic when the user clicks the save button.

```javascript
document.getElementById('saveButton').addEventListener('click', () => {
  chrome.tabs.query({ active: true, currentWindow: true }, (tabs) => {
    const tab = tabs[0];
    if (tab && tab.id) {
      chrome.scripting.executeScript({
        target: { tabId: tab.id },
        function: savePageContent
      });
    }
  });
});

function savePageContent() {
  // Get the entire document as text
  const content = document.documentElement.outerHTML;

  // Save the content to local storage or send it back to the popup
  chrome.runtime.sendMessage({ action: 'saveContent', content });
}
```

5. **Create the background service worker** (`background.js`): This script listens for messages from the popup and can handle saving the content to a more permanent storage like IndexedDB or sending it to a server.

```javascript
chrome.runtime.onMessage.addListener((message, sender, sendResponse) => {
  if (message.action === 'saveContent') {
    // Here you would typically save the content to a database or send it to a server
    console.log('Saving content:', message.content);

    // For demonstration purposes, we just log the content
    sendResponse({ status: 'success' });
  }
});
```

6. **Add icons**: You should add some icons to your extension. Place them in an `icons` folder within your project directory.

7. **Load the extension into Chrome**: Go to `chrome://extensions/`, enable Developer Mode, and click on "Load unpacked". Select the root directory of your extension.

This basic setup allows you to save the content of the current webpage by clicking a button in the extension's popup. The actual implementation details may vary depending on how you want to store or process the saved content.

