Next, we use the `Gl.use_program` function to specify which program should be used for rendering. We set the values of the uniforms `n`, `a`, `b`, and `c` using the `Gl.uniform1i` and `Gl.uniform1fv` functions.

Finally, we dispatch the compute shader using the `Gl.dispatch_compute` function, specifying the number of work groups to execute. After that, we use the `Gl.memory_barrier` function to ensure that the results are visible to other parts of the program.

